## Root cause

k3d's internal containerd has no mirror/auth for these registries:
- `cr.kgateway.dev` (kgateway)
- `cr.fluentbit.io` (fluent-bit)
- `registry.k8s.io` (kube-state-metrics)
- `nn-docker-remote.artifactory.insim.biz` direct pull (postgresql — has it as a mirror endpoint for docker.io but not as a standalone pull target)

`amp-api` and `amp-db-migration` are in `Init:0/1` waiting for postgresql — they'll unblock automatically.

## Fix: pull on host, sideload into k3d

The host Docker daemon has Artifactory mirrors configured; k3d containerd doesn't.
`k3d image import` bypasses containerd pull entirely.

```bash
# Step 1: pull on the host
docker pull cr.kgateway.dev/kgateway-dev/kgateway:v2.2.1
docker pull cr.fluentbit.io/fluent/fluent-bit:4.2.3
docker pull busybox
docker pull registry.k8s.io/kube-state-metrics/kube-state-metrics:v2.18.0
docker pull nn-docker-remote.artifactory.insim.biz/bitnami/postgresql:16
```

If `cr.fluentbit.io` is blocked on the host too, use the docker.io alias:
```bash
docker pull fluent/fluent-bit:4.2.3
docker tag fluent/fluent-bit:4.2.3 cr.fluentbit.io/fluent/fluent-bit:4.2.3
```

```bash
# Step 2: sideload into k3d
k3d image import \
  cr.kgateway.dev/kgateway-dev/kgateway:v2.2.1 \
  cr.fluentbit.io/fluent/fluent-bit:4.2.3 \
  busybox \
  registry.k8s.io/kube-state-metrics/kube-state-metrics:v2.18.0 \
  nn-docker-remote.artifactory.insim.biz/bitnami/postgresql:16 \
  -c amp-local

# Step 3: delete stuck pods so kubelet restarts them against the local image
kubectl delete pod kgateway-7dcf4bf945-ldbsv          -n openchoreo-control-plane
kubectl delete pod fluent-bit-5tfx4                    -n openchoreo-observability-plane
kubectl delete pod kube-state-metrics-6fbd956566-sz25q -n openchoreo-observability-plane
kubectl delete pod amp-postgresql-0                    -n wso2-amp
```

After postgresql starts, watch amp-api and amp-db-migration come up on their own:
```bash
kubectl get pods -n wso2-amp -w
```